{t: Whole Lotta Love}
{st: Led Zeppelin}
{key: E}
{tempo: 90}

{sot: Intro}
| E5          | E5          | E5          | E5          |
{eot}

{sot: Riff}
| E5    D5 E5 | E5    D5 E5 | E5    D5 E5 | E5    D5 E5 |
{eot}

{sot: Verse}
| E5    D5 E5 | E5    D5 E5 | E5    D5 E5 | E5    D5 E5 |
| E5    D5 E5 | E5    D5 E5 | E5    D5 E5 | E5    D5 E5 |
{eot}

{sot: Chorus}
| A5          | A5          | E5    D5 E5 | E5    D5 E5 |
{eot}

{sot: Solo}
| E5          | E5          | E5          | E5          |
{eot}

{sov: Notes}
Hard Rock Cornerstone: Built on Jimmy Page's iconic syncopated riff in E Blues /
E Pentatonic, featuring the characteristic low E string pick-up slide into the D5-E5 stab.

Riff Mechanics: Palm-mute the repeating open low E string notes, then release the
mute sharply on the fast D5 to E5 power chord resolution.

Chorus Accent: The chorus breaks the single-note groove with heavy, open A5 power
chord stabs behind Robert Plant's lead vocal line.

Freakout / Solo Section: The middle section breaks into ambient, experimental
theremin and tape-echo soundscapes over Bonham's freeform percussion before
re-entering on Page's isolated, unaccompanied pickup guitar solo.
{eov}